WEBVTT

00:36.161 --> 00:38.955
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

00:46.921 --> 00:48.506
You crazy bastard.

00:49.132 --> 00:51.885
Do you have a death wish?
Why would you drink after a flu shot?

00:51.968 --> 00:53.678
This is why you're so wasted.

00:53.762 --> 00:56.347
Didn't the doctor tell you not to drink?

00:57.223 --> 00:58.850
-They did.
-"They did."

00:58.933 --> 01:00.351
You've got to be kidding me.

01:01.770 --> 01:05.482
Hey, your mouth is still full.
Finish it before eating more.

01:06.399 --> 01:08.735
It tastes better when I have a mouthful.

01:10.445 --> 01:11.821
-Jeez.
-You're unbelievable.

01:13.782 --> 01:15.742
What are you, a beggar? Don't eat that!

01:15.825 --> 01:17.077
-Don't eat that!
-Why?

01:17.160 --> 01:18.787
-Hey!
-No!

01:20.497 --> 01:21.581
I'm a beggar!

01:25.210 --> 01:26.252
Hey, where's Jin-man?

01:26.336 --> 01:28.129
He's on the night shift,
so he won't be home.

01:28.213 --> 01:29.923
Awesome, that's great.

01:30.006 --> 01:31.174
Is he handsome?

01:31.257 --> 01:33.968
-Do you two look alike?
-Would you rather I did or didn't?

01:34.052 --> 01:36.554
-I hope you two are twins.
-Hello.

01:37.764 --> 01:39.182
Hello.

01:41.476 --> 01:42.519
Hello.

01:53.530 --> 01:56.950
All right, we're in a safe zone now.

01:57.033 --> 01:58.076
It's Hwang Dong-man's place!

01:58.159 --> 01:59.994
-Wow.
-I'm going to look around.

02:00.078 --> 02:01.329
Eun-a, coats go over there.

02:01.412 --> 02:02.872
You're so pretty.

02:04.290 --> 02:05.625
Look at this.

02:05.708 --> 02:07.877
It's the director's office.

02:07.961 --> 02:09.337
Come on over.

02:10.004 --> 02:11.297
What's this?

02:14.717 --> 02:16.344
You must be the one.

02:16.427 --> 02:19.222
The one Hwang Dong-man
borrowed from a loan shark for.

02:20.306 --> 02:21.182
Tangerine?

02:22.142 --> 02:24.352
-You're good at communicating with it.
-Can I feed it?

02:30.358 --> 02:32.235
What is he doing?

02:32.318 --> 02:33.987
-Hwang Dong-man!
-Yes?

02:34.070 --> 02:35.738
To commemorate your visit here,

02:36.573 --> 02:37.407
you each get a towel.

02:37.490 --> 02:39.075
Oh, thank you.

02:39.159 --> 02:40.577
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

02:40.660 --> 02:42.120
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

02:42.203 --> 02:43.538
Thank you for coming.

02:43.621 --> 02:44.706
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

02:44.789 --> 02:46.583
"Park Jin-bun's
80th Birthday Celebration"?

02:47.208 --> 02:48.793
Who's Park Jin-bun?

02:48.877 --> 02:50.712
-Probably someone's mother.
-Right?

02:50.795 --> 02:51.796
It's someone's mother, right?

02:51.880 --> 02:52.755
Oh, come on!

02:53.339 --> 02:55.633
Hey, there's no ketchup.

02:55.717 --> 02:58.177
We need ketchup with potato chips.

02:58.261 --> 02:59.804
-Ketchup, please.
-Hold on.

02:59.888 --> 03:01.264
-Do you have ketchup?
-Of course!

03:02.557 --> 03:03.474
We have…

03:05.226 --> 03:07.103
a seven-year-old bottle of ketchup.

03:07.186 --> 03:08.980
-What? Seven years old?
-Yeah.

03:09.856 --> 03:10.690
Oh my.

03:13.776 --> 03:15.236
Ta-da.

03:27.874 --> 03:28.791
Let's see.

03:29.792 --> 03:31.419
It says 2018!

03:31.502 --> 03:32.921
-It really is seven years old.
-Seriously?

03:33.004 --> 03:34.589
-Yeah.
-It's totally fine.

03:34.672 --> 03:35.506
No, don't…

03:35.590 --> 03:36.758
-Really?
-What the heck?

03:36.841 --> 03:38.927
-It's still fine.
-Oh my gosh.

03:40.053 --> 03:41.221
Hey!

03:41.304 --> 03:42.222
It really is fine.

03:42.305 --> 03:43.890
-It's fine.
-It's fine.

03:43.973 --> 03:45.099
It tastes just fine.

03:45.183 --> 03:46.142
Why is it still fine?

03:46.226 --> 03:48.144
Don't eat too quickly, okay?

03:48.228 --> 03:50.271
Do you know how hard it is
to age this for seven years?

03:50.355 --> 03:51.522
We need a photo of this.

03:51.606 --> 03:54.442
The "2018" faded a bit,
so it looks like "2016."

03:55.944 --> 03:57.278
Hey, hold it steady.

03:57.362 --> 03:59.239
I need a good shot of the date.

04:03.243 --> 04:04.202
What's that?

04:04.285 --> 04:05.286
What are you doing?

04:05.370 --> 04:06.746
Just hold on a second.

04:06.829 --> 04:08.331
TOP 10 TV SHOWS IN SOUTH KOREA
I'LL LOVE ANYONE THIS WINTER

04:08.873 --> 04:10.250
It's a hit.

04:10.333 --> 04:12.377
I'll Love Anyone This Winter
topped the streaming charts.

04:13.336 --> 04:15.296
-Congratulations to you
-Congratulations.

04:15.380 --> 04:17.215
Congratulations to you

04:17.298 --> 04:19.050
-Congrats on topping the streaming charts
-Congratulations.

04:19.133 --> 04:21.427
-Congratulations to you
-Congratulations.

04:24.514 --> 04:26.849
I thought I'd calm down if I got drunk,
but I haven't.

04:28.017 --> 04:29.602
Has she lost her damn mind?

04:29.686 --> 04:31.437
The drama is out right now.

04:31.521 --> 04:34.440
So why did she post a couple photo
and pull people out of the story?

04:34.524 --> 04:35.566
Sure enough,

04:35.650 --> 04:37.652
someone commented, "Behave yourself."

04:37.735 --> 04:39.070
So I liked the comment.

04:39.988 --> 04:42.448
Then she DMed me and chewed me out.

04:42.532 --> 04:44.242
-Did I do something wrong?
-No.

04:44.826 --> 04:46.786
The drama is out,
so she should behave herself.

04:46.869 --> 04:47.829
-Right.
-Right.

04:47.912 --> 04:48.955
Plus, it's a rom-com.

04:49.038 --> 04:50.832
-Exactly!
-You know what?

04:51.457 --> 04:52.750
When someone comes at us hard,

04:54.002 --> 04:55.253
our hearts sink, and we think,

04:55.336 --> 04:56.754
"Did I do something wrong?"

04:56.838 --> 04:58.381
We blame ourselves too easily.

04:59.549 --> 05:00.466
Self-reflection

05:01.467 --> 05:02.719
is the language of the weak.

05:03.511 --> 05:05.722
Have you ever seen bad people
reflect on their actions?

05:06.347 --> 05:07.598
Don't reflect on this.

05:08.099 --> 05:10.518
-Don't reflect.
-Right. I won't reflect.

05:10.601 --> 05:12.103
-I won't.
-Hey.

05:12.186 --> 05:14.230
You have to open your eyes.

05:14.314 --> 05:16.274
You can't do that with your eyes closed.

05:16.357 --> 05:17.650
What are you doing?

05:18.651 --> 05:19.610
Hey!

05:20.153 --> 05:22.071
-Oh jeez.
-Here.

05:22.655 --> 05:24.115
Whatever.

05:29.203 --> 05:30.788
What's it to you where I am?

05:31.956 --> 05:33.916
-Who is it?
-Ms. Oh Jeong-hui.

05:34.500 --> 05:38.212
Ms. Oh Jeong-hui is no different
than any other mother, is she?

05:38.296 --> 05:40.256
I guess she also checks
what time her daughter will be home.

05:42.341 --> 05:45.094
Can I ask you something?
I'm genuinely curious.

05:47.430 --> 05:50.266
How's Ms. Oh's relationship
with her biological daughter?

05:51.893 --> 05:52.810
I don't know.

05:52.894 --> 05:54.312
Do they keep in touch?

05:54.395 --> 05:55.396
I don't know.

05:55.480 --> 05:57.065
It's taboo to talk about her.

05:57.148 --> 05:58.191
Why?

05:58.274 --> 05:59.317
How should I know?

06:00.735 --> 06:03.362
But I have a feeling

06:04.155 --> 06:05.740
that they ended on very bad terms.

06:06.532 --> 06:09.410
Not that divorces
usually end on good terms,

06:10.078 --> 06:11.537
but I think the daughter
took her dad's side.

06:13.247 --> 06:14.832
I'd like to see her, though.

06:17.668 --> 06:18.503
Why?

06:19.003 --> 06:19.921
Just because.

06:20.797 --> 06:22.632
She probably knows who I am,

06:22.715 --> 06:24.008
but I don't know who she is.

06:24.592 --> 06:25.968
Isn't that kind of unfair?

06:26.052 --> 06:27.804
It really is unfair.

06:27.887 --> 06:30.056
-Seriously.
-How old is she?

06:30.139 --> 06:31.891
I don't know anything.

06:31.974 --> 06:34.185
Oh, I know her name. It's Byeon Si-on.

06:35.144 --> 06:37.522
I once overheard her on the phone.

06:38.856 --> 06:40.441
-Byeon Si-on?
-Yeah.

06:41.484 --> 06:42.318
Wait.

06:43.486 --> 06:44.695
Byeon Si-on.

06:45.571 --> 06:46.405
Eun-a…

06:47.031 --> 06:49.826
Eun-a was going to change her name
to Byeon Si-on.

06:50.368 --> 06:51.369
What?

06:52.495 --> 06:54.038
No, no, no.

06:54.122 --> 06:56.040
Nope. That's just wrong.

06:56.124 --> 06:56.958
Not Byeon Si-on.

06:57.542 --> 06:59.836
Byeon Eun-a has to stay Byeon Eun-a.

06:59.919 --> 07:01.003
-Byeon Eun-a.
-Yeah.

07:01.087 --> 07:03.089
-Byeon Eun-a is so much better.
-Right.

07:03.172 --> 07:05.216
-Right.
-Ms. Byeon Eun-a.

07:05.299 --> 07:08.302
Please don't become Byeon Si-on.

07:09.303 --> 07:11.222
-Byeon Eun-a!
-Byeon Eun-a!

07:11.305 --> 07:13.182
-Byeon Eun-a!
-Byeon Eun-a!

07:13.266 --> 07:14.684
-Byeon Eun-a!
-Byeon Eun-a!

07:14.767 --> 07:15.601
Hey.

07:16.227 --> 07:18.563
Let me hold onto that.

07:27.572 --> 07:28.698
DAYS LIKE THIS, DAYS LIKE THAT
POEMS BY HWANG JIN-MAN

07:28.781 --> 07:29.657
Come on.

07:29.740 --> 07:33.244
SOMEWHERE, A WRONG REMAINS
POEMS BY HWANG JIN-MAN

07:33.327 --> 07:35.246
Why do you keep messing with that?

07:35.329 --> 07:36.956
Do you want me to help you?

07:37.039 --> 07:38.624
Oh, well…

07:39.417 --> 07:40.376
This…

07:42.044 --> 07:44.547
SOMEWHERE, A WRONG REMAINS
POEMS BY HWANG JIN-MAN

07:48.092 --> 07:48.926
Oh.

07:49.802 --> 07:50.887
They don't look alike.

07:50.970 --> 07:53.014
POET HWANG JIN-MAN

07:53.097 --> 07:54.390
He's handsome.

08:28.174 --> 08:29.592
My feet are cold!

08:33.930 --> 08:36.182
Mi-ran, you have to come see this.

08:36.265 --> 08:37.642
-Come quickly and see this.
-Okay.

08:37.725 --> 08:39.352
This is really cool.

08:39.852 --> 08:41.854
I promise it's really cool. Just watch.

08:42.480 --> 08:44.232
All right, just watch.

08:45.358 --> 08:46.692
-Help him!
-Hey!

08:47.568 --> 08:49.570
-You know what this is, right?
-No.

08:49.654 --> 08:51.072
-Watch carefully, okay?
-Okay.

08:51.155 --> 08:53.074
-One, two, three!
-Two, three!

08:59.247 --> 09:02.166
-Merry Christmas!
-Merry Christmas!

09:02.250 --> 09:05.002
-Three, two, one!
-Three, two, one!

09:05.086 --> 09:06.128
Action!

09:07.755 --> 09:08.839
Merry Christmas!

09:27.316 --> 09:28.234
It's snowing.

09:54.677 --> 09:55.970
I'm so happy

09:57.388 --> 10:00.725
to have relationships like this
where we can be crazy together.

10:40.931 --> 10:44.393
KNOCK KNOCK KNOCK
BY MA JAE-YEONG, YEONG-SIL

10:52.485 --> 10:53.319
Good night.

11:15.633 --> 11:17.051
You're back. Eat before you wash up.

11:25.142 --> 11:26.102
Yes, sir?

11:26.727 --> 11:27.561
Oh.

11:27.645 --> 11:29.397
We're not starting right away.

11:30.439 --> 11:31.816
It'll take some time.

11:32.817 --> 11:33.859
We're still casting.

11:34.735 --> 11:35.820
Yes, of course.

11:36.612 --> 11:38.322
The end of the year
is peak catering season,

11:38.406 --> 11:39.407
so of course I'll work.

11:39.990 --> 11:40.991
Yes, sir.

11:41.075 --> 11:41.992
Salute!

11:47.581 --> 11:49.250
Don't get too caught up in life.

11:52.711 --> 11:54.255
Don't get caught up in happiness…

11:55.965 --> 11:57.508
or sadness either.

12:09.854 --> 12:11.313
Can't I get a little caught up?

12:12.189 --> 12:13.399
It's the first time I've been happy.

12:24.493 --> 12:26.954
Don't run the washing machine
early in the morning!

12:28.539 --> 12:30.833
The pipes are frozen,
so the water won't drain!

13:10.206 --> 13:11.582
CEO KO

13:17.129 --> 13:18.047
Why are you calling so early?

13:18.130 --> 13:19.131
Ms. Ko.

13:19.215 --> 13:21.300
You need to work smarter than this.

13:22.092 --> 13:23.010
What's wrong with you?

13:24.512 --> 13:27.056
I heard you gave Noh Kang-sik
Hwang Dong-man's screenplay.

13:27.139 --> 13:28.933
Did you do that
because you think you've got a shot?

13:29.016 --> 13:30.267
Mr. Choi, do you like me?

13:30.351 --> 13:31.894
Why do you keep pestering me?

13:31.977 --> 13:34.104
Do you regret our falling out?

13:34.188 --> 13:35.523
I find it satisfying.

13:35.606 --> 13:36.857
Watch what you say.

13:36.941 --> 13:38.609
Pester you? When did I ever do that?

13:38.692 --> 13:40.611
Let's be clear,
you're the ones pestering me.

13:41.737 --> 13:45.241
You gave Noh Kang-sik that screenplay
just to get on my nerves.

13:45.324 --> 13:46.909
Please shut up

13:47.451 --> 13:49.161
and mind your own business.

13:49.245 --> 13:52.122
There are only so many top actors.
How am I supposed to avoid yours?

13:52.206 --> 13:54.166
I just pitch it everywhere I can
and take what sticks.

13:54.250 --> 13:56.752
-Hey.
-If you call me again,

13:57.461 --> 13:59.129
I'll assume you like me.

14:02.550 --> 14:03.676
It's too early for this.

14:07.555 --> 14:08.639
I want that satisfaction

14:09.265 --> 14:11.225
of slamming down the receiver,

14:11.809 --> 14:14.270
but I can't get that with a cell phone!

14:14.353 --> 14:15.271
That son of a--

14:15.354 --> 14:16.188
Ms. Ko!

14:17.273 --> 14:19.149
The screen will crack.

14:28.784 --> 14:31.370
I won't abandon you guys.

14:31.453 --> 14:34.123
I'll come here to teach
even after an all-night shoot.

14:34.206 --> 14:36.500
-So brace yourselves, okay?
-Okay!

14:38.544 --> 14:39.587
Who's the lead actor?

14:39.670 --> 14:40.754
Who do you want it to be?

14:40.838 --> 14:41.922
Ji Seung-u!

14:42.006 --> 14:43.215
-Lee Gi-jun.
-Moon Seong-a?

14:43.299 --> 14:44.216
Cho Min-seong!

14:44.300 --> 14:45.634
Noh Kang-sik!

14:46.218 --> 14:47.052
Bingo.

14:47.636 --> 14:49.680
Of course, I'm fully aware how busy he is.

14:52.057 --> 14:53.767
He's the country's top actor, after all.

15:01.817 --> 15:03.027
I'll make you another cup.

15:04.194 --> 15:05.029
You know how it is.

15:05.654 --> 15:08.073
It's best that you get back to us quickly,
even if it's a pass.

15:08.157 --> 15:10.409
We can't wait long for Mr. Noh Kang-sik.

15:10.492 --> 15:11.827
Since it's a government-funded project,

15:11.911 --> 15:13.579
we have to submit
quarterly progress reports

15:13.662 --> 15:14.830
to get the payments.

15:16.040 --> 15:17.374
Yes, that's how it is.

15:17.458 --> 15:19.001
Please ask him one more time.

15:21.420 --> 15:23.213
Yes, thank you. Goodbye.

15:25.215 --> 15:28.135
I'll send a screenplay over
and hear nothing back.

15:28.218 --> 15:31.805
This must be a big dilemma for you,
Gyeong-se.

15:32.681 --> 15:36.226
Hwang Dong-man needs to fail,
but Ko Hye-jin needs to do well.

15:36.310 --> 15:38.437
-How is that a dilemma?
-How is that a dilemma?

15:46.153 --> 15:47.655
You're saying Dong-man needs to fail.

15:49.615 --> 15:50.991
-No.
-Too late.

15:53.327 --> 15:55.704
You didn't bring him in to make money.

15:55.788 --> 15:56.956
You were pissed at Mr. Choi

15:57.039 --> 16:00.084
and just decided to do something else,
even if it's Hwang Dong-man's.

16:00.167 --> 16:02.169
You really think I'd just take on
a random screenplay?

16:03.337 --> 16:05.172
You read his screenplay.

16:05.255 --> 16:07.758
-So what if the writing is good?
-At least it's good!

16:13.180 --> 16:14.014
You hate it that much?

16:14.765 --> 16:17.142
You really hate seeing
Hwang Dong-man do well?

16:17.226 --> 16:19.228
Even though it means I'd do well too?

16:23.315 --> 16:25.943
You know the saying, "When your cousin
buys land, you turn green with envy"?

16:26.026 --> 16:27.653
I bet it only exists in Korea.

16:27.736 --> 16:29.363
It exists everywhere!

16:29.446 --> 16:30.948
Don't put down our people like that.

16:31.031 --> 16:33.409
I'm your wife, not your cousin!

16:33.492 --> 16:35.119
Your wife wants to buy some land!

16:35.202 --> 16:37.371
-We've always been poor anyway.
-For crying out loud.

16:37.454 --> 16:38.372
Cham, cham, cham.

16:42.334 --> 16:44.169
I'm going to become rich,

16:44.878 --> 16:46.630
so go ahead and stay poor.

16:59.143 --> 17:01.562
How do you fail to dodge it
every single time?

17:02.146 --> 17:03.981
I always turn to the right.

17:06.191 --> 17:07.651
Call it a voluntary punishment.

17:11.947 --> 17:16.326
I talked to Hye-jin about crediting you
for the screenplay adaptation.

17:18.537 --> 17:20.456
That violates credit guidelines.

17:21.081 --> 17:23.333
You can't get credit
for simply giving notes.

17:23.959 --> 17:25.753
You should be the only one credited.

17:26.754 --> 17:28.172
But you wrote all those comments.

17:29.631 --> 17:30.716
It doesn't work that way.

17:31.925 --> 17:33.010
I wish

17:33.594 --> 17:35.429
I could just let the whole world know

17:36.138 --> 17:38.265
what kind of writer you are.

17:39.016 --> 17:40.309
If this turns out well,

17:40.392 --> 17:43.020
I'm going to go around telling people,
"Byeon Eun-a did this!"

17:43.103 --> 17:46.148
"Byeon Eun-a did this!"

17:46.231 --> 17:49.568
I'm going to cover the whole world
with Byeon Eun-a.

17:55.574 --> 17:56.909
Hello!

17:56.992 --> 17:58.035
Hello.

18:07.169 --> 18:08.378
It's been a long time.

18:09.505 --> 18:10.756
I wanted to show my gratitude.

18:10.839 --> 18:12.674
Thanks to you, My Mother was a success.

18:12.758 --> 18:16.428
Ms. Oh prepared gifts
to thank everyone for their hard work.

18:16.512 --> 18:17.763
Oh my.

18:18.388 --> 18:20.224
What brings you here?
You didn't call ahead.

18:20.307 --> 18:22.684
I've been meaning to stop by,
but I only now got around to doing so.

18:22.768 --> 18:25.312
I didn't get to properly thank everyone
for their hard work.

18:25.395 --> 18:27.689
You're the one who did all the hard work.

18:28.398 --> 18:29.316
This way, please.

18:29.399 --> 18:30.400
Oh, Director Ma.

18:31.652 --> 18:32.486
Mr. Choi.

18:34.154 --> 18:34.988
Who's this?

18:35.072 --> 18:37.658
Oh, this is Director Ma Jae-yeong.

18:37.741 --> 18:39.118
You read his screenplay,
Knock knock knock.

18:39.201 --> 18:40.202
I see.

18:40.828 --> 18:42.746
-Hello.
-Nice to meet you.

18:43.497 --> 18:45.082
I enjoyed your screenplay.

18:47.417 --> 18:48.377
Thank you.

18:51.296 --> 18:52.256
Let's go in.

19:01.140 --> 19:03.350
WE ARE SORRY TO SHARE THAT DIRECTOR
KIM SEONG-JUN'S MOTHER HAS PASSED AWAY

19:06.728 --> 19:08.272
RECENTS

19:08.355 --> 19:09.982
LEE JUN-HWAN

19:11.942 --> 19:14.361
I just got a funeral notice
from Director Kim.

19:15.195 --> 19:16.488
When are you going to the funeral hall?

19:17.739 --> 19:19.116
-There's more.
-Oh gosh.

19:19.199 --> 19:21.118
-Oh wow.
-Thank you.

19:21.201 --> 19:22.035
Thank you.

19:24.705 --> 19:26.957
Doesn't she have an insane presence?

19:27.040 --> 19:29.084
Her figure is amazing for her age.

19:29.168 --> 19:30.878
She's so generous.

19:30.961 --> 19:32.296
Oh Jeong-hui is the best.

19:33.755 --> 19:36.717
"People are all masses of emotion."

19:36.800 --> 19:38.135
I totally agree.

19:40.262 --> 19:42.139
How did you come up
with something like that?

19:47.728 --> 19:48.770
You're right.

19:49.396 --> 19:52.399
If there were no such thing
as good parents or bad parents

19:52.482 --> 19:54.943
and all humans were born
from a bamboo shoot

19:55.027 --> 19:57.905
with no one to blame or resent,
this would be heaven.

19:58.989 --> 20:01.825
How did the gods miss something so simple?

20:07.331 --> 20:10.000
All the lines were words
I wanted to feel on my lips,

20:10.083 --> 20:11.501
so I read them out loud.

20:14.963 --> 20:16.632
There was real depth in your writing.

20:16.715 --> 20:20.177
You're more on the feminine side
than the masculine side, right?

20:21.803 --> 20:23.096
Do you have a woman's fortune?

20:23.180 --> 20:24.431
-Do you?
-Oh gosh, no.

20:24.932 --> 20:26.892
Why did you write the protagonist as male?

20:30.520 --> 20:33.232
The screenplay would work just fine
with a female protagonist.

20:34.066 --> 20:35.192
A woman fits better.

20:36.068 --> 20:37.402
You can't pull off

20:38.028 --> 20:39.780
this screenplay with just acting.

20:39.863 --> 20:42.574
You need an actor
who already carries that sentiment.

20:43.200 --> 20:46.745
Don't assume you can explain everything
and guide them on set.

20:47.329 --> 20:50.457
To do it justice, you need an actor
who understands the depth of your writing

20:50.540 --> 20:53.669
and can deliver every nuance
with microscopic precision.

20:54.253 --> 20:56.630
You'll have trouble if you cast an actor

20:56.713 --> 20:58.674
who makes every film their own
with their acting style.

21:00.259 --> 21:02.177
You clearly gave it your all.

21:02.261 --> 21:05.597
Can you handle
watching everything fall apart on set

21:05.681 --> 21:06.890
with an actor like that?

21:11.478 --> 21:13.355
I understood Knock knock knock

21:14.439 --> 21:15.649
to its core.

21:37.546 --> 21:39.631
There's no need to find someone
to front the contract for you.

21:39.715 --> 21:42.592
I'll sign the contract under my name
and pay you your screenplay fee myself.

21:50.600 --> 21:52.352
BYEON EUN-A

21:56.606 --> 21:57.816
Don't leave me on read.

21:57.899 --> 21:59.401
Just say you got it.

22:24.634 --> 22:27.721
I told you to go home. Why did you come?

22:27.804 --> 22:29.473
There's nothing to do there all alone.

22:30.557 --> 22:31.433
How are you feeling?

22:31.516 --> 22:33.101
I feel better than yesterday.

22:33.685 --> 22:34.519
Where's the caregiver?

22:35.353 --> 22:37.064
I told them to go eat.

22:38.565 --> 22:40.609
How much money are you spending?

22:41.234 --> 22:43.070
Surgery bills and now caregiver expenses…

22:43.153 --> 22:45.322
I'm spending it so you can live longer.

22:45.405 --> 22:46.406
Just live a long life.

22:46.490 --> 22:48.366
My goodness.

22:49.034 --> 22:50.535
By the way, who sent that?

22:52.621 --> 22:54.164
I thought it was you.

23:00.587 --> 23:01.963
WISHING YOU A SPEEDY RECOVERY
CEO PARK SANG-JIN

23:04.257 --> 23:06.885
NAME: BYEON SI-ON
GUARDIAN: GA SU-JA

23:29.658 --> 23:31.576
-Oh, hello.
-Hey, Yeong-su.

23:31.660 --> 23:32.577
-It's been a while.
-It has.

23:32.661 --> 23:33.787
-How have you been?
-Good.

23:34.830 --> 23:36.373
-Hello.
-Dong-man.

23:36.456 --> 23:37.916
I heard your film got greenlit.

23:37.999 --> 23:39.167
Oh, yes.

23:39.251 --> 23:42.003
Wow, your luck has finally turned.
Congratulations.

23:42.587 --> 23:43.755
Thank you.

23:49.052 --> 23:50.428
I heard the first two episodes are done.

23:51.054 --> 23:51.972
When do you start filming?

23:52.055 --> 23:53.682
How should I know that?

23:53.765 --> 23:55.100
If the director doesn't know, who does?

23:55.684 --> 23:57.394
I can't find any available actors.

23:57.477 --> 24:00.021
The good ones are booked solid
for the next couple of years.

24:00.605 --> 24:03.191
As long as the writing is good,
who cares about the actors?

24:03.275 --> 24:05.986
-Do calligraphers care what brush to use?
-They care. They care a lot.

24:06.069 --> 24:08.280
The more skilled they are,
the more expensive their brushes.

24:08.363 --> 24:10.157
Actors are everything in a movie.

24:12.492 --> 24:14.452
Then why'd you send your screenplay
to Noh Kang-sik?

24:16.371 --> 24:17.664
I respect actors

24:17.747 --> 24:21.877
like Noh Kang-sik and Oh Jeong-hui
whose names are now proper nouns.

24:21.960 --> 24:22.794
The rest are just…

24:22.878 --> 24:24.462
You mean common nouns.

24:25.172 --> 24:26.214
Common nouns.

24:26.298 --> 24:28.466
Names are already proper nouns.

24:28.550 --> 24:30.177
Whenever I say something, you just…

24:30.260 --> 24:32.387
Then stop talking like you know everything
when you're wrong.

24:32.470 --> 24:33.889
You just don't like me.

24:33.972 --> 24:34.931
Does anyone like you?

24:35.515 --> 24:36.600
Byeon Eun-a.

24:38.143 --> 24:39.519
Who likes you?

24:40.604 --> 24:41.771
Ko Hye-jin?

24:41.855 --> 24:44.274
She probably liked you
a long, long, long time ago.

24:45.817 --> 24:48.403
-Hey, say hello.
-It's been a while.

24:48.486 --> 24:49.446
-Hello.
-Hello.

24:49.529 --> 24:51.489
You two were inseparable in college.

24:51.573 --> 24:52.782
You still are, huh?

24:52.866 --> 24:56.036
Come on now, that was ages ago.

24:56.119 --> 24:57.621
These two are sworn enemies now.

25:02.125 --> 25:03.710
-Hello, sir.
-It's okay.

25:03.793 --> 25:04.920
-Sit down.
-Hello, sir.

25:05.629 --> 25:06.504
-Sit down.
-Hello.

25:11.968 --> 25:12.802
Hey.

25:13.303 --> 25:14.387
He beat up another one.

25:15.347 --> 25:16.181
Who?

25:17.307 --> 25:18.600
Cha Jeong-min.

25:19.267 --> 25:22.646
If his co-star acts well, he beats them
and knocks them off their game.

25:22.729 --> 25:25.315
There's no way he actually beat them up
in this day and age.

25:25.941 --> 25:28.526
Maybe he didn't full-on beat him up,
but he must've put his hands on him.

25:29.110 --> 25:29.986
You know?

25:33.114 --> 25:35.116
-There you are.
-Hey.

25:35.200 --> 25:37.535
-You can sit here.
-Thanks.

25:37.619 --> 25:39.246
Thank you for coming.

25:40.121 --> 25:40.956
Oh man.

25:41.039 --> 25:43.833
Gyeong-se, I hear you're doing
a streaming series.

25:44.584 --> 25:45.961
You never know until it starts.

25:46.044 --> 25:48.630
Hey, we need to start adapting now.

25:48.713 --> 25:50.173
The film era is basically over.

25:50.799 --> 25:52.300
Dong-man, I heard your film got greenlit.

25:53.051 --> 25:54.511
-Sorry?
-Your film.

25:55.262 --> 25:56.388
-Yes.
-That's good.

25:56.471 --> 25:57.847
All that waiting has paid off.

25:57.931 --> 26:00.100
-Take care of your health.
-Thank you.

26:03.353 --> 26:04.813
Your mother's well, right?

26:08.525 --> 26:09.484
Dong-man.

26:10.485 --> 26:12.487
You're at my mother's funeral.

26:16.032 --> 26:17.242
Did you just come for the food?

26:29.629 --> 26:31.298
That disrespectful punk.

26:31.381 --> 26:32.757
Come on, Kang-sik.

26:32.841 --> 26:34.384
Keep it friendly.

26:34.467 --> 26:35.719
"Keep it friendly"?

26:36.386 --> 26:37.762
Keep what friendly?

26:37.846 --> 26:41.474
Why should I keep it friendly
with someone who can't even act?

26:44.686 --> 26:48.481
He doesn't even have the basics.
Mainstream actor, my ass.

26:52.360 --> 26:53.194
Hello.

26:55.989 --> 26:57.198
We met not too long ago.

26:58.366 --> 26:59.451
In front of Agit.

27:01.578 --> 27:02.662
We shook hands.

27:07.125 --> 27:08.293
So what?

27:10.378 --> 27:12.297
I came to formally introduce myself.

27:15.216 --> 27:16.509
I'm Hwang Dong-man.

27:16.593 --> 27:17.510
Hwang Dong-man.

27:18.553 --> 27:20.930
I really want to make this film with you.

27:23.850 --> 27:24.684
Listen.

27:27.187 --> 27:29.314
There's a proper way to approach someone.

27:29.397 --> 27:32.108
Do I need to respond to everyone
who comes at me?

27:32.817 --> 27:34.569
I have an agency, you know.

27:35.820 --> 27:36.905
Oh.

27:36.988 --> 27:38.656
We sent this to your agency,

27:38.740 --> 27:39.824
but we haven't heard back.

27:41.576 --> 27:43.495
I really want to make this film with you.

27:44.079 --> 27:46.623
So you're basically saying,

27:46.706 --> 27:48.124
"I want to succeed."

27:48.208 --> 27:49.584
"Please help me."

27:49.667 --> 27:50.502
Why?

27:51.711 --> 27:53.838
Why should I help you?

27:56.299 --> 27:57.258
Do you know me?

27:59.010 --> 28:00.470
Have we worked on anything together?

28:02.555 --> 28:03.598
What films have you done?

28:05.392 --> 28:06.810
What films have you done?

28:12.315 --> 28:14.234
Well, nothing yet.

28:15.735 --> 28:18.279
This is my debut film.

28:20.198 --> 28:21.616
Know your place.

28:22.158 --> 28:23.618
I get your ambition,

28:23.701 --> 28:25.620
but I've got my own too.

28:25.703 --> 28:28.081
Do you know how hard I worked
to get to where I am?

28:28.164 --> 28:30.166
Why would I team up
with a nobody like you?

28:33.253 --> 28:35.004
If you want to work with me…

28:37.674 --> 28:38.758
move up

28:39.384 --> 28:40.343
to where I am.

28:42.178 --> 28:44.556
But for now, just stay where you are

28:44.639 --> 28:46.933
and stick to those on your level.

28:49.018 --> 28:51.813
Kids these days have too much ambition

28:51.896 --> 28:53.314
and just come at you.

28:56.735 --> 28:58.278
You should leave now.

29:02.741 --> 29:04.451
You have a lot of money.

29:05.660 --> 29:06.494
You want to borrow some?

29:06.578 --> 29:09.289
If I were set for life,

29:10.081 --> 29:12.292
I'd just take on whatever comes my way

29:13.960 --> 29:16.880
instead of getting into ego clashes
with much younger juniors.

29:18.882 --> 29:20.717
Why not just work with me

29:21.760 --> 29:23.261
before you get canceled
for beating a junior?

29:23.970 --> 29:24.971
-Go away.
-Get up.

29:25.054 --> 29:25.889
Get up.

29:27.557 --> 29:31.352
Nothing is more entertaining
than your mug!

29:31.436 --> 29:33.480
Let's see it full screen!

29:33.563 --> 29:35.315
-Not on a phone!
-You idiot!

29:35.398 --> 29:37.400
On a big screen!

29:37.484 --> 29:38.902
What the hell are you doing?

29:39.611 --> 29:40.445
Hey.

29:40.528 --> 29:42.739
"Weather Maker"?

29:42.822 --> 29:44.199
What are you, a god?

29:45.408 --> 29:46.242
Crazy bastard.

29:51.247 --> 29:52.081
Hey.

30:02.300 --> 30:03.760
He must be out of his mind.

31:06.698 --> 31:08.157
Isn't this pretty much the best

31:09.242 --> 31:11.494
for a directing team office?

31:11.578 --> 31:13.413
Given the rent, of course, it's the best.

31:13.496 --> 31:14.622
What a great view.

31:16.040 --> 31:17.750
What did DP Choi Gi-yeong say?

31:17.834 --> 31:19.168
-Is he on board?
-Yes.

31:19.252 --> 31:20.295
Nice.

31:20.378 --> 31:23.673
I used all the connections I had
to persuade him.

31:23.756 --> 31:24.632
Very well.

31:24.716 --> 31:26.175
We have a solid key crew.

31:26.926 --> 31:28.261
Now we just wait for it to become a hit.

31:29.304 --> 31:30.513
I'll do my best.

31:33.725 --> 31:34.642
So?

31:34.726 --> 31:35.977
Have you thought about it?

31:37.562 --> 31:38.688
About what Oh Jeong-hui said.

31:39.439 --> 31:40.315
Right.

31:42.692 --> 31:44.027
What do you think, Mr. Choi?

31:44.110 --> 31:46.487
The director's opinion matters the most.

31:50.158 --> 31:51.326
I think Noh Kang-sik

31:52.785 --> 31:54.370
might end up taking the lead on set,

31:54.454 --> 31:56.414
and I don't know if I can handle him.

31:57.040 --> 32:00.668
I think we need an actor
who fully understands the writing.

32:02.795 --> 32:04.130
And isn't Noh Kang-sik

32:05.214 --> 32:06.257
a bit of a risk?

32:07.050 --> 32:08.343
He's always getting into trouble.

32:15.642 --> 32:17.477
Let's put a hold
on Noh Kang-sik's contract.

32:19.646 --> 32:20.521
Okay.

32:21.147 --> 32:22.732
By the way, the screenplay fees

32:22.815 --> 32:24.651
will go to Ma Jae-yeong,
and he'll pay Yeong-sil.

32:24.734 --> 32:26.235
He said Yeong-sil suggested it.

32:27.195 --> 32:29.072
You really think Yeong-sil suggested that?

32:29.155 --> 32:30.740
It was probably Ma Jae-yeong.

32:31.991 --> 32:34.243
Oh Jeong-hui has an uncanny knack
for reading screenplays,

32:34.327 --> 32:36.955
and she said
the writing felt distinctly feminine.

32:37.038 --> 32:38.790
Yeong-sil wrote it.

32:39.749 --> 32:40.750
Just leave it be.

32:42.502 --> 32:44.462
Don't say a word about Yeong-sil,

32:45.213 --> 32:46.631
or it'll set Ma Jae-yeong off.

33:22.166 --> 33:24.085
How many names do you have?

33:25.253 --> 33:27.338
Byeon Si-on, Byeon Eun-a…

33:29.340 --> 33:30.383
and Yeong-sil.

33:33.511 --> 33:35.304
I can tell it's you.

33:36.139 --> 33:37.348
My name is Byeon Eun-a.

33:37.432 --> 33:38.808
Yeong-sil is a pseudonym.

33:38.891 --> 33:41.102
-Did you choose "Eun-a" as your name?
-Yes.

33:43.563 --> 33:45.523
Of all the names, why choose Eun-a?

33:45.606 --> 33:47.984
Of all the names, why choose Si-on?

33:48.776 --> 33:49.819
You named me, right?

33:50.403 --> 33:52.572
It sounds sophisticated and special.

33:53.823 --> 33:55.033
So?

33:55.700 --> 33:57.201
You're not even Christian.

33:58.161 --> 33:59.787
Why give your newborn a name

34:00.872 --> 34:03.124
that makes it sound like
they're forced to be special?

34:05.543 --> 34:06.794
Isn't it natural

34:07.420 --> 34:09.797
to want your child
to become someone special?

34:10.548 --> 34:12.300
Some parents name their child "Yeong-sil"

34:12.383 --> 34:14.135
so they'll have an easygoing life.

34:17.180 --> 34:18.890
Husband or child,

34:19.599 --> 34:23.227
everything tied to you had to be special
so you could stand out.

34:24.020 --> 34:25.980
But when you looked at
your quiet, slow child,

34:27.565 --> 34:30.151
your eyes suggested
things weren't quite right.

34:31.652 --> 34:32.987
I still remember that look.

34:34.155 --> 34:35.031
So you ended up

34:36.741 --> 34:38.576
giving up both your husband and child.

34:41.037 --> 34:42.872
It's ambition when you're capable.

34:43.873 --> 34:45.374
It's greed when you're not.

34:46.417 --> 34:48.753
If I'm clearly capable,

34:49.754 --> 34:52.048
why should I crush my ambitions
and hold myself back?

34:53.800 --> 34:55.384
You seem more fake to me.

34:56.552 --> 34:58.721
You have ambition. You're just killing it.

34:59.722 --> 35:01.224
You want people to know you're Yeong-sil.

35:01.849 --> 35:03.017
You want people to know

35:03.101 --> 35:05.019
how big your part was
in writing Knock knock knock.

35:05.645 --> 35:08.439
At the same time,
you're afraid people will tear you apart,

35:08.523 --> 35:12.735
so you hide behind a pseudonym
while feeding your ego.

35:12.819 --> 35:13.653
Right?

35:15.738 --> 35:19.325
I bet you're in hell right now
because you want to reveal yourself.

35:20.118 --> 35:22.829
And because you can't stand
Ma Jae-yeong taking all the credit.

35:26.499 --> 35:27.458
Just go for it.

35:28.126 --> 35:29.669
Tell everyone you're Yeong-sil

35:29.752 --> 35:31.003
and Oh Jeong-hui's daughter.

35:33.589 --> 35:35.633
I hear you've been
acting out of line with Mr. Choi.

35:36.676 --> 35:39.428
Would you really be able to act that way
if it weren't for me?

35:40.263 --> 35:42.974
"That's right,
keep giving me a hard time."

35:43.057 --> 35:45.852
"I'll make sure
you're utterly embarrassed later."

35:47.728 --> 35:49.397
You're saying that didn't cross your mind?

35:54.235 --> 35:56.112
You seem more fake to me.

36:22.096 --> 36:23.764
You said you were going to be
really successful.

36:24.348 --> 36:26.642
You told me not to cling to you then
and act like we're close.

36:27.602 --> 36:31.856
You told me not to leech off
your shining success.

36:33.274 --> 36:34.525
When will you ever shine

36:35.276 --> 36:36.903
if you hide behind a pseudonym?

36:47.079 --> 36:48.456
-Hi, Mi-ran.
-Hello.

36:48.539 --> 36:50.208
-Hello.
-Hello.

36:50.791 --> 36:51.876
So?

36:51.959 --> 36:54.128
-So--
-Aren't you going to say hi?

36:59.800 --> 37:00.801
Hello.

37:02.637 --> 37:03.971
So, what does he like about you?

37:04.055 --> 37:04.889
What?

37:07.016 --> 37:08.392
Hey, that's a secret.

37:08.476 --> 37:09.936
-I can't believe you asked me that.
-Come on.

37:10.019 --> 37:12.396
Tell me more.

37:12.480 --> 37:13.314
My gosh.

37:13.397 --> 37:15.566
-I'm so jealous.
-This is hilarious.

37:18.527 --> 37:20.363
I'm so jealous.

37:22.531 --> 37:23.991
Oh my gosh.

37:24.575 --> 37:25.743
Sounds like it was fun.

37:25.826 --> 37:26.786
It was really fun.

37:26.869 --> 37:29.538
-It's a secret, okay?
-Okay, okay.

37:42.635 --> 37:43.928
Did you learn how to laugh yesterday?

37:45.346 --> 37:47.932
You laugh way too hard,
like you've never done it before.

37:48.599 --> 37:50.142
Do you laugh like that all the time?

37:50.643 --> 37:52.645
Because it seems like you only do it
when I show up.

37:53.980 --> 37:55.523
I always laugh a lot.

37:58.317 --> 37:59.151
Look.

37:59.235 --> 38:01.112
We're not on good terms,

38:01.195 --> 38:02.947
so shouldn't you behave yourself?

38:04.031 --> 38:06.534
Viewers are telling you to behave yourself
and stop acting out.

38:08.035 --> 38:09.495
Did I ever tell you

38:10.121 --> 38:11.998
that I almost became a shaman?

38:12.081 --> 38:13.833
I still see things, you know.

38:13.916 --> 38:15.960
You should really be careful

38:16.043 --> 38:17.378
because I see trouble in your future.

38:18.129 --> 38:21.632
I can see
you're just dying to cause trouble.

38:22.591 --> 38:24.844
You see, women who gain recognition
as someone's girlfriend

38:24.927 --> 38:30.057
instead of through their own work
eventually start acting overly confident,

38:30.141 --> 38:32.560
as if their boyfriend's name is their own.

38:39.442 --> 38:41.861
If you want to stay known
as someone's girlfriend,

38:42.653 --> 38:44.822
watch yourself
before things get out of hand.

38:52.246 --> 38:53.205
You know,

38:55.291 --> 38:59.503
I think people who claim
they can see things are so obnoxious.

39:01.172 --> 39:02.840
They should worry about their own future.

39:04.842 --> 39:07.094
There are rumors
in the Korean community in New York

39:07.970 --> 39:09.972
that Chairman Jang
is living with another woman.

39:11.223 --> 39:13.559
The only reason
anyone even acknowledges you

39:13.642 --> 39:15.061
is because you're Oh Jeong-hui's daughter.

39:16.479 --> 39:18.606
But I wonder who will
once she's out of your life.

39:21.442 --> 39:22.735
What does it feel like?

39:22.818 --> 39:24.820
Your father is living with another woman,

39:25.488 --> 39:28.824
but you're living under the same roof
with your stepmother.

39:29.658 --> 39:30.701
Oh, I see.

39:31.702 --> 39:34.538
Is that why you latch onto any man?

39:34.622 --> 39:36.374
Because you've got no one to love?

39:36.999 --> 39:39.502
You should be ashamed and embarrassed

39:39.585 --> 39:41.504
for latching onto
someone else's boyfriend.

39:45.466 --> 39:46.926
Let go. You'd better let go!

39:47.009 --> 39:49.595
I've dreamed about
grabbing you by the hair.

39:49.678 --> 39:51.222
Your hair feels freaking amazing!

39:51.305 --> 39:52.473
You crazy bitch.

39:55.351 --> 39:57.520
I grew up showered with love.

39:57.603 --> 40:00.481
My grandmother
goes to early morning prayers for me,

40:00.564 --> 40:02.274
gets me herbal tonics every season,

40:02.358 --> 40:04.026
and still dotes on me!

40:04.110 --> 40:06.487
-I've got so much love I can't hold it in!
-Don't do this!

40:06.570 --> 40:08.239
I'm overflowing with love!

40:10.783 --> 40:12.493
Is it a crime to have so much love?

40:12.576 --> 40:14.912
If I were you,
I'd be hugging me and crying,

40:14.995 --> 40:17.540
upset that I couldn't share that bastard,
Jeong Hyeon-u.

40:18.040 --> 40:20.418
You think you won? Are you happy now?

40:21.043 --> 40:23.754
You know what's so stupid
about what you believe?

40:24.630 --> 40:28.134
Thinking that loving more
makes you weaker.

40:28.217 --> 40:29.635
Idiot.

40:29.718 --> 40:31.262
That's why you're pathetic.

40:31.345 --> 40:33.139
You can't even tell the difference
between acting and reality,

40:33.222 --> 40:34.765
you crazy bitch!

40:34.849 --> 40:35.808
Hey.

40:35.891 --> 40:37.017
Let go.

40:37.810 --> 40:38.853
Hey.

40:40.062 --> 40:40.938
Goddamn it.

40:49.989 --> 40:50.865
Get in.

40:51.907 --> 40:54.869
I'm going to make you pay for this,
you crazy bitch!

40:54.952 --> 40:56.787
Go ahead and try, you dumbass bitch!

41:08.174 --> 41:10.968
We got the CCTV footage,
so we'll be seeing you soon.

41:11.051 --> 41:12.428
Okay. See you soon.

41:28.527 --> 41:29.695
Let's talk later.

41:51.800 --> 41:52.843
Let's go.

41:53.427 --> 41:54.386
Action!

42:16.492 --> 42:17.910
They can't release the CCTV footage.

42:19.495 --> 42:22.122
We collected plenty on them too
when they threatened to report you

42:22.206 --> 42:23.666
for stalking.

42:24.875 --> 42:25.960
They've got a lot of problems.

42:26.961 --> 42:28.671
Don't worry. They won't release it.

42:36.804 --> 42:38.722
Let's keep up
the celebrity mother-daughter angle

42:39.807 --> 42:40.766
to the very end.

43:00.160 --> 43:01.036
Jin-man.

43:01.745 --> 43:02.955
What's your purpose in life?

43:11.213 --> 43:12.214
To live lightly.

43:16.760 --> 43:18.846
Letting go of everything I can…

43:21.056 --> 43:23.350
not forming deep attachments to anything…

43:26.604 --> 43:27.730
and living lightly.

44:56.985 --> 44:57.820
Everyone

44:59.029 --> 45:00.656
probably struggled to write these.

45:03.117 --> 45:04.284
But no one reads them…

45:06.537 --> 45:07.871
and they just get thrown away.

45:10.124 --> 45:11.333
What's the point of all this?

45:12.668 --> 45:14.545
Everything disappears in the end anyway.

45:29.810 --> 45:30.853
So why…

45:34.064 --> 45:35.941
are we living such hard lives…

45:39.903 --> 45:41.905
as if we'll never disappear?

46:05.846 --> 46:06.680
As if…

46:08.265 --> 46:09.850
we'll never disappear.

46:12.978 --> 46:13.854
As if…

46:14.938 --> 46:15.939
we'll never…

46:17.149 --> 46:18.358
disappear.

47:07.574 --> 47:09.409
Hey, Dong-man!

47:11.495 --> 47:13.163
Hwang Dong-man!

47:14.122 --> 47:16.416
Everything my voice reaches

47:16.500 --> 47:17.334
is mine.

47:20.587 --> 47:22.130
Hey, Eun-a!

47:25.300 --> 47:27.094
Byeon Eun-a!

47:31.265 --> 47:33.350
Hey, Dong-man!

47:34.351 --> 47:36.311
Hey, Eun-a!

47:43.652 --> 47:45.904
He was going around acting like
he was going to work with Noh Kang-sik.

47:45.988 --> 47:47.531
-Serves him right.
-You punk.

47:47.614 --> 47:48.907
Are you Hwang Dong-man now?

47:49.491 --> 47:51.618
-Finding joy in others' failures?
-Didn't you know?

47:51.702 --> 47:53.328
I'm the Dong-man
of the freshman class of 2008.

47:54.663 --> 47:55.664
I'm so sick of this.

47:55.747 --> 47:58.584
I want everyone around me to do well.

47:58.667 --> 48:00.210
If I'm not going to make it anyway,

48:00.294 --> 48:03.088
the people around me should succeed
so I can pick up the crumbs.

48:04.047 --> 48:06.341
I like picking up the crumbs.

48:07.676 --> 48:09.970
Why doesn't anyone consider
picking up the crumbs?

48:10.053 --> 48:12.264
It's no good if none of us make it.

48:12.347 --> 48:16.101
Someone around me has to succeed
so I can live off it.

48:17.978 --> 48:18.812
Is she a good writer?

48:19.396 --> 48:21.523
-No.
-How could you say that?

48:21.607 --> 48:23.317
It's not my fault I can't write.

48:23.400 --> 48:25.736
But I can inspire instead.

48:25.819 --> 48:27.487
Put this crazy woman to use!

48:28.905 --> 48:30.532
Right, put her to use.

48:30.616 --> 48:32.868
Put her to good use!

48:32.951 --> 48:34.786
Put her to use.

48:34.870 --> 48:36.872
I have too much pride

48:36.955 --> 48:39.166
to live off picking up the crumbs.

48:39.249 --> 48:43.003
I'd rather sell my soul
and buy talent instead!

48:43.086 --> 48:46.089
Just sell an arm.
Why would you sell your soul?

48:46.173 --> 48:47.883
You don't even know if it exists.

48:47.966 --> 48:50.302
If it could be sold,
I'd sell it countless times.

48:50.927 --> 48:51.970
It's simple.

48:52.054 --> 48:54.389
Just sell an arm or don't.

48:54.473 --> 48:55.766
This is faster for Koreans.

48:55.849 --> 48:56.725
What about this?

48:57.684 --> 48:59.686
If giving up an arm

48:59.770 --> 49:02.147
makes you the world's top director,

49:02.814 --> 49:03.857
would you sell it or not?

49:05.275 --> 49:08.820
-The world's top director, huh?
-Top?

49:17.037 --> 49:18.080
I'd sell it.

49:18.163 --> 49:20.957
You said you'd live off
picking up the crumbs.

49:21.541 --> 49:23.585
That's because I have no talent.

49:23.669 --> 49:25.962
If I had talent, why would I do that?

49:30.050 --> 49:31.468
-Sell it?
-Did you see that look?

49:32.260 --> 49:34.638
What the heck?
Did she already sell her arm?

49:34.721 --> 49:35.597
Who would buy it?

49:36.181 --> 49:38.684
I could write a different version
of Sister Vengeance.

49:40.102 --> 49:41.812
You don't have to sell your arm.

49:42.896 --> 49:43.980
I read the script.

49:44.981 --> 49:47.359
The lines are much better
than Director Park's usual lame ones.

49:50.404 --> 49:51.822
Keep up the good work.

49:51.905 --> 49:56.368
I'd sell my arm if that's what it takes
to make him a huge success.

49:59.037 --> 50:01.915
He's the most adorable person ever.

50:08.672 --> 50:09.506
Do you want him?

50:17.097 --> 50:18.515
Goodness, Ms. Ko.

50:20.976 --> 50:22.060
No, it's not like that.

50:29.151 --> 50:30.444
There they are.

50:30.527 --> 50:32.404
I'm going to go now.

50:32.487 --> 50:34.740
-Wait up!
-Let's go together.

50:34.823 --> 50:36.491
-Let's go together.
-Hey, wait up.

50:37.159 --> 50:38.618
See you at home.

50:38.702 --> 50:40.454
You must have an early morning meeting.

51:06.021 --> 51:07.063
Hello.

51:10.066 --> 51:10.901
Oh.

51:11.693 --> 51:13.153
I'm Jang Mi-ran.

51:13.236 --> 51:16.072
The one who sang at your cousin's wedding.

51:21.787 --> 51:22.829
It's like art

51:24.414 --> 51:27.083
Who knew this day would come?
It's like art

51:29.795 --> 51:30.921
I guess you didn't see it.

51:35.300 --> 51:36.343
I just…

51:39.805 --> 51:41.389
I just wanted to see you.

51:44.226 --> 51:47.395
I wondered what kind of person
could write poems like that.

51:47.896 --> 51:50.732
SOMEWHERE, A WRONG REMAINS
POEMS BY HWANG JIN-MAN

52:06.748 --> 52:09.835
It's for uncovering the truth for me.

52:11.545 --> 52:12.796
A token of thanks, if you will.

52:46.037 --> 52:47.414
I wash my face

52:48.915 --> 52:50.250
But something won't come off

52:51.251 --> 52:52.961
I trim my nails

52:54.296 --> 52:56.256
But something can't be trimmed

52:58.550 --> 53:02.178
I wring out a wet rag and wipe the floor

53:04.097 --> 53:05.557
But something won't wipe off

53:07.309 --> 53:08.685
Somewhere

53:10.770 --> 53:11.605
A wrong remains…

53:13.398 --> 53:14.232
A wrong remains…

53:20.530 --> 53:22.115
I set the table and sit down

53:24.284 --> 53:25.785
I see a glass

53:30.957 --> 53:31.791
Yes

53:32.459 --> 53:33.418
It's a drink

53:57.734 --> 53:58.652
Hey, Ax.

53:59.945 --> 54:00.904
Get in here.

54:01.446 --> 54:04.324
Nobody has a problem
changing the protagonist to a woman.

54:04.407 --> 54:07.327
But you just had to dig in your heels
and make the meeting uncomfortable.

54:07.410 --> 54:09.496
Are the other producers morons?

54:09.579 --> 54:11.373
Do I have to rethink this
because you disagree?

54:11.456 --> 54:12.958
Even the director approved!

54:13.041 --> 54:14.417
Are you a writer?

54:15.085 --> 54:18.546
You went on about how Knock knock knock
isn't that kind of a story.

54:18.630 --> 54:20.256
You need to know when to stop.

54:21.132 --> 54:24.886
You review others' work long enough,
and you start thinking you're a writer.

54:25.595 --> 54:27.597
Do you know how writing is created?

54:28.098 --> 54:30.350
You want to try writing for a month
under Yeong-sil?

54:30.433 --> 54:33.103
You want a brutal reality check
on your skill level?

54:33.812 --> 54:35.939
Everyone wants to become a writer.

54:36.022 --> 54:39.818
People with no talent always go nuts
over someone else's good writing

54:39.901 --> 54:41.611
and act like they know everything,
as if they wrote it.

54:41.695 --> 54:43.697
They practically foam at the mouth.

54:43.780 --> 54:45.949
Just focus on your own work,

54:46.032 --> 54:49.452
and stop being a smart-ass
with that half-baked skill of yours!

54:49.536 --> 54:50.453
Got it, Ax?

54:56.167 --> 54:57.377
I'm Yeong-sil.

55:01.339 --> 55:02.215
It's me.

55:03.800 --> 55:04.801
I'm Yeong-sil.

55:09.764 --> 55:12.100
The writer Ma Jae-yeong
is so desperate to hide.

55:52.599 --> 55:54.517
NOH KANG-SIK

55:59.731 --> 56:01.566
The person you are trying to reach
is unavailable.

56:01.649 --> 56:02.942
You will be redirected to voicemail after…

56:03.026 --> 56:05.612
-This damn bastard.
-Stop calling.

56:06.863 --> 56:07.697
Kang-sik.

56:10.950 --> 56:12.202
This is the second time

56:13.912 --> 56:15.121
he offered a role and took it back.

56:20.752 --> 56:21.920
Hi, hi, hi!

56:22.003 --> 56:23.129
-Hey.
-You're here.

56:24.255 --> 56:25.340
Hello.

56:29.385 --> 56:30.261
I'll have a beer.

56:30.345 --> 56:31.596
Is that all the clothes he has?

56:41.106 --> 56:43.525
Let me tell you a story about this coat--

56:43.608 --> 56:45.401
You told that story a million times.

56:45.485 --> 56:47.362
-He's right.
-But he hasn't heard it yet.

56:47.445 --> 56:48.780
Just drink. Here you go.

56:49.489 --> 56:50.740
Hey!

56:51.616 --> 56:55.328
This right here took part in World War II.

56:56.704 --> 56:58.915
Do you see this bullet hole?

56:59.541 --> 57:04.212
I wear the clothes of a Russian soldier
who stood in the center of world history,

57:04.295 --> 57:06.214
where bullets flew all around him!

57:06.798 --> 57:11.886
This is a symbol of my intent
to step into the center of history myself!

57:11.970 --> 57:13.263
And my resolve!

57:13.346 --> 57:14.973
Which is why

57:15.056 --> 57:18.017
I wear this every single day.

57:18.643 --> 57:20.353
As long as I'm wearing this,

57:20.436 --> 57:22.439
it's impossible to hurt me

57:22.522 --> 57:24.941
with words like "low-level nobody."

57:25.024 --> 57:26.818
You can say anything you want,

57:26.901 --> 57:29.320
but nothing will scratch me.

57:31.489 --> 57:34.284
This right here stopped a bullet
in the middle of a war.

57:35.034 --> 57:38.705
Do you think mere human words
could hurt it?

57:41.374 --> 57:42.667
Good job.

57:42.750 --> 57:44.919
-Nicely done.
-Great job.

57:45.003 --> 57:46.588
-Well done.
-Here, have a drink.

57:46.671 --> 57:48.173
Hurry and eat first.

57:48.256 --> 57:50.008
There's a story
behind everything he carries.

57:50.675 --> 57:52.302
His laptop belonged to his late father.

57:52.385 --> 57:55.013
He gets his shoes from a shop
he's frequented for 20 years.

57:55.722 --> 57:57.348
He's addicted to stories.

57:58.016 --> 58:00.810
Life is nothing without stories.

58:00.894 --> 58:03.563
You might as well be dead without stories.

58:03.646 --> 58:05.899
He's more like a beggar than a director.

58:05.982 --> 58:06.816
Man.

58:07.442 --> 58:08.860
I can already see the set.

58:08.943 --> 58:12.280
I have zero interest in doing well.

58:12.363 --> 58:13.948
I'm going to fail completely

58:14.032 --> 58:16.701
and take pride
in simply having made a film.

58:16.784 --> 58:19.078
And I'm going to wish everyone
who lost money investing in me

58:19.162 --> 58:23.666
great success and wealth
for generations to come

58:23.750 --> 58:26.336
and pray for them every day.

58:27.921 --> 58:30.173
As for the ones who totally blew me off,

58:30.256 --> 58:32.050
I hope they crash and burn!

58:37.013 --> 58:39.641
I'm going to pray really hard.

58:39.724 --> 58:41.059
"Please fail."

58:41.142 --> 58:42.185
"Please fail."

58:42.268 --> 58:44.354
I'm going to pray for their failure,

58:44.437 --> 58:45.813
and even perform a shamanistic ritual!

58:45.897 --> 58:49.234
I may not perform a shamanistic ritual
for my own success,

58:49.984 --> 58:52.695
but I'll do it for others' failures.

58:52.779 --> 58:54.364
I'll take out a loan if I have to!

58:54.447 --> 58:55.657
Stop already, you punk!

58:55.740 --> 58:57.408
Just stop, okay?

58:57.492 --> 58:59.160
-That's enough.
-Why?

58:59.244 --> 59:00.870
-It's fun.
-Okay, okay.

59:00.954 --> 59:02.163
-It's fine as long as it's fun.
-All right.

59:02.247 --> 59:04.207
This is the story of my life.

59:04.290 --> 59:06.251
Okay, I got it. Just lower your voice.

59:07.252 --> 59:09.420
-I suddenly want to do it.
-You like blockbuster hits?

59:10.171 --> 59:12.173
-What's the point of being rich
-His film.

59:12.257 --> 59:14.133
if your life story sucks?

59:14.217 --> 59:17.762
If I had that kind of money,
I'd totally live in style!

59:18.388 --> 59:19.389
What was your name again?

59:20.056 --> 59:22.100
It's Hwang Dong-man!

59:23.184 --> 59:24.227
I'll work with you.

59:28.147 --> 59:29.649
Let's do it, Hwang Dong-man.

59:30.441 --> 59:31.609
What are you doing, Kang-sik?

59:31.693 --> 59:33.736
You haven't even read the screenplay.

59:33.820 --> 59:35.488
I don't have to. He's too obvious.

59:36.406 --> 59:38.616
It'll run me into the ground,
and I'll go through hell.

59:40.118 --> 59:42.245
Let me try writing a different life story.

59:42.829 --> 59:43.830
Let's just go for it.

59:44.956 --> 59:46.583
Let's team up with a guy like him

59:47.667 --> 59:48.960
and just go for it.

59:53.590 --> 59:56.509
-Hold on.
-Please don't, sir.

59:59.304 --> 01:00:00.138
I'm serious.

01:00:01.681 --> 01:00:02.765
I'll do it.

01:00:03.391 --> 01:00:04.225
Let's do it.

01:00:05.351 --> 01:00:06.769
I'll take half my usual fee.

01:00:10.356 --> 01:00:12.066
It's government-funded, right?

01:00:13.526 --> 01:00:14.444
So half my usual fee.

01:00:15.361 --> 01:00:16.654
Strike while the iron's hot, right?

01:00:17.363 --> 01:00:18.323
Should we sign a contract?

01:00:18.406 --> 01:00:19.365
Let's do that.

01:00:20.575 --> 01:00:21.451
Bring the contract.

01:00:38.259 --> 01:00:39.719
Ms. Ko, slow down. You'll get hurt.

01:00:39.802 --> 01:00:41.679
Hurry up. Come on.

01:00:42.180 --> 01:00:43.890
ACTOR CONTRACT

01:00:48.311 --> 01:00:49.312
Sir.

01:00:49.937 --> 01:00:51.272
You're drunk right now.

01:00:52.482 --> 01:00:53.483
Don't sign it.

01:01:11.668 --> 01:01:14.671
NOH KANG-SIK

01:01:22.095 --> 01:01:24.055
Good for you!

01:01:26.140 --> 01:01:27.141
Thank you, sir!

01:01:55.336 --> 01:01:56.421
Come on.

01:02:05.263 --> 01:02:06.097
Thank you.

01:02:09.225 --> 01:02:10.601
Let's step into the center

01:02:11.227 --> 01:02:12.061
of history.

01:02:13.521 --> 01:02:14.355
Okay.

01:02:36.669 --> 01:02:38.463
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

01:02:56.564 --> 01:02:58.441
Make it big, Hwang Dong-man!

01:02:58.524 --> 01:03:02.111
Now that Noh Kang-sik is on board,
I'm worried it might be too successful.

01:03:03.571 --> 01:03:06.449
Let's keep the fact that you're Yeong-sil
just between you and me.

01:03:06.532 --> 01:03:09.160
I heard the writer
is against casting me in the role.

01:03:09.243 --> 01:03:11.329
I'd like to know why you're against it,

01:03:11.913 --> 01:03:13.247
Ms. Yeong-sil.

01:03:13.331 --> 01:03:16.292
Who the hell are you
to object to casting Oh Jeong-hui?

01:03:16.375 --> 01:03:18.628
You even went behind my back
and told Mr. Choi that you're Yeong-sil.

01:03:18.711 --> 01:03:19.837
Call them now!

01:03:19.921 --> 01:03:21.589
-Let go of me!
-Hey.

01:03:21.672 --> 01:03:24.383
Call the reporters,
but at least wait until after my film!

01:03:24.967 --> 01:03:26.719
Wait until I'm done with my film!

01:03:26.803 --> 01:03:31.724
Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
